  cletus Jethro
  @cletus_jethro • Dec 19
  The initial blast speed is PETN's detonation
  velocity of 8400 m/s. Thus, the speed drop over
  1 foot is 8400 - 309 = 8091 m/s.
  To arrive at the solution:
  1. Calculate E = mx heat of detonation =
  0.003 × 5.81 × 106 = 1.743 × 104 J.
  2. Compute
  (p/E)1/2 = 1.225/17430 ~ 0.00838 s/m?
  3. Adjust r/E = 0.3048/1.035 = 0.2945.
  4. Compute (r/E)5/2 = (0.2945)2.5 ~ 0.047.
  5. Find t = 0.047 × 0.00838 ~ 3.94 × 10-4 s.
  6. Compute v =
  (2/5) x (0.3048/3.94 x 10-4) = 309 m/s.
  7. Subtract from initial detonation velocity:
  8400 - 309 = 8091 m/s.
